# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What is committed, and why.
#
# exports/            IS COMMITTED. It used to be `.raw/` and used to hold the
#                     unscrubbed n8n exports, which must never reach a remote.
#                     Those files have now been scrubbed IN PLACE by
#                     `.tooling/scrub.py`, so what is on disk is the sanitised
#                     export, and the sanitised export is the canonical diffable
#                     artefact: it is what `.tooling/extract-units.py` reads, and
#                     it is what you diff against the live n8n instance to see
#                     what drifted. Ignoring it would throw away the only
#                     reviewable record of the workflows. Keep it in git.
#
#                     Corollary: never re-export a workflow straight into
#                     exports/ and commit. Re-export, then run
#                     `.tooling/scrub.py`, then `.tooling/leak-check.sh`, then
#                     commit. The leak check is the gate.
#
# workflows/*.md      Committed. Prose specs. Scrubbed.
# harness/, fixtures/ Committed. Test scaffolding and scenarios. Scrubbed.
# .tooling/           Committed, including scrub-map.json -- which holds the REAL
#                     literals as its keys. That is deliberate (the scrub cannot be
#                     re-applied or audited without them) and leak-check.sh excludes
#                     that one file. It is also the reason this repo is private and
#                     must not be pushed to a public remote. See docs/decisions.md (c).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Never commit an unscrubbed export. If you need somewhere to stage one before
# scrubbing, use these; they are ignored.
.raw/
exports-unscrubbed/
*.unscrubbed.json
*.raw.json

# Transient only.
node_modules/
scratch/
*.log
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local editor / OS noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Test output
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# Orca / local dev — never commit these
*.bundle
.mcp.json

# Orca task loop — transient trigger files. The automation lives in tools/orca/
# (committed); the task cards and journal are local scratch.
tasks/inbox/
tasks/queued/
tasks/done/
tasks/journal.txt

# Orca Fast Lane — the coordinator's control files, written into the worktree
# root by tools/orca/fastlane.ps1 and by the agents it starts. Local scratch for
# one run: the task card, the DeepSeek test-leg result, the orchestrator DONE
# file. Never committed.
.fastlane-*
